  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Practices for Family Farming</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASSESOAR will work in eight municipalities in southeastern Paran to train 2,000 farmers and public officials in the development and application of (1) &quot;agricultural forests&quot; (agroflorestais), which combine agricultural production and forest management for economic and environmental benefit; (2) low-cost, low-maintenance silos; and (3) cisterns that catch and store rainwater. Through workshops, exchanges and brochures, an additional 25,000 Brazilians will become familiar with the new techniques. (BR-860)</narrative>
  </description>
